        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Work Orders at Risk Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "WORK_ORDERS_AT_RISK_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1767811799006",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767811799008_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Use `WorkOrderList`: {{$context.$variables.WorkOrderList}} to generate the summary.\n\n- If `WorkOrderList` is null or empty, return:  \n  No past due or missing assignments work orders found in the time period.\n- Do not ask for clarification or user input if no events are present. Only display the message.\n\nWhen data is present:\n- Define at-risk as either:\n  - Missing Assignments: `MissingAssignmentFlag` is true (labor assignments needed)\n  - Past Due: `PastDueFlag` is true (completion date is in the past)\n\n**Output Rules (must follow exactly):**\n- Write a newspaper-style headline of fewer than 30 words.\n- Base your summary on the content of `WorkOrderDescription` to assess resource constraints. Do not reference or mention the description in your output.\n- For past due work orders that are not high priority (`WorkOrderPriority` not 1), suggest rescheduling lower priority work orders.\n- Output only the headline.  \n- Do NOT output anything else.\n\n**Strict:**  \nNo other words, punctuation, quotes, or formatting.  \nNo lists, no tables, no JSON, no explanations.  \nNo work order numbers, organization/asset IDs, or dates.  \nNever display any internal identifier."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Work Orders at Risk"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_WORK_ORDERS_AT_RISK",
          "id": "1767817652764",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767817652765_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Use `WorkOrderList`: {{$context.$variables.WorkOrderList}} for displaying the results.\n- Organization Code: {{$context.$variables.OrganizationCode}}\n- Organization ID: {{$context.$variables.OrganizationId}}\n\n- If `WorkOrderList` is null or empty, return a `messageListWidget` with:\n  - `title`: No at risk work orders\n  - `summary`: No work orders matched the criteria for past-due status or missing labor assignments in the selected time period.\n  - `badgeText`: INFO\n  - `priority`: medium\n- Do not ask for clarification or request user input if no events are present. Only display the message.\n\n**Rules:**\n- Priority summary:\n   - Derive from `WorkOrderPriority`.\n   - Only consider work orders with PastDueFlag `true` when forming priority summary for Past-due Work Orders\n   - Only consider work orders with MissingAssignmentFlag `true` when forming priority summary for Work Orders Missing Assignments\n   - If all work orders have the same priority, state: `Priority: [count] [priority]`.\n   - If priorities are mixed, state: `Priority: [count1] High, [count2] Medium, [count3] Low`.\n   - Lower numeric values represent higher priority (1 = highest).\n   - Null or empty priorities should be considered Low. Assign ranges for High, Medium, and Low as appropriate based on your data.\n\n**messageListWidget Sections:**\n\n1. Past-due Work Orders:\n   - `title`: Past-due work orders — [{{$context.$variables.PastDueCount}}]\n   - `subtitle`: Planned completion date before {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} • [priority summary]\n   - `summary`: Explain in business language why these work orders are at risk (do not mention specific work orders or formulas).\n   - `badgeText`: Past-due\n   - `timestamp`: leave empty\n\n2. Work Orders Missing Assignments:\n   - `title`: Missing assignments — [{{$context.$variables.MissingAssignmentsCount}}]\n   - `subtitle`: Pending resource assignments • [priority summary]\n   - `summary`: Explain in business language why these assignments are needed (do not mention specific work orders or formulas).\n   - `badgeText`: Resource assignments\n   - `timestamp`: leave empty\n   - Generate an AdditionalAction:\n      - `followUpCommand`: ora.Invoke(actionResourceAssignmentNav, {\"OrganizationId\": \"{{$context.$variables.OrganizationId}}\", \"OrganizationCode\": \"{{$context.$variables.OrganizationCode}}\"})\n      - `actionText`: Manage\n\n- Set the overall `title` as: At Risk Work Orders, indicating the time range from {{$context.$variables.StartDate}} to {{$context.$variables.EndDate}} in natural language, without specific dates, where current date is {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} . eg. `At-Risk Work Orders — Recent Backlog (Last 30 Days) & Imminent Risk (Next 7 Days)`\n\n- Do not include internal identifiers (such as IDs) or extra commentary.\n\n- Return only the messageListWidget and actionable insights."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "At Risk Work Order Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "AT_RISK_WORK_ORDER_DETAILS",
          "id": "1768274795408",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768274795410_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Use `WorkOrderList`: {{$context.$variables.WorkOrderList}} for displaying results.\n- Organization Code: {{$context.$variables.OrganizationCode}}\n- Organization ID: {{$context.$variables.OrganizationId}}\n- If `WorkOrderList` is null or empty, return:  \n  No past due or missing assignments work orders found in the time period.\n- Do not ask for clarification or request user input if no events are present.\n\n**Formatting Instructions:**  \n- Show up to 25 rows from `WorkOrderList` in the original order.\n- For each work order, display these fields:\n  - Work Order (`WorkOrderNumber`)\n  - Description (`WorkOrderDescription`; wrap text if needed)\n  - Asset Number (`AssetNumber`)\n  - Priority (`WorkOrderPriority`)\n  - Planned Completion (`PlannedCompletionDate`, formatted as YYYY-MM-DD)\n  - Past Due (`PastDue`, show as \"Yes\" or \"No\")\n  - Assignment Status  \n    - Display as a badge  as per value of `AssignmentStatus`\n      - `priority: alert` for \"unassigned\"  \n      - `priority: warning` for \"partially assigned\"  \n      - `priority: success` for \"assigned\"  \n      - for empty string `\"\"` leave blank.\n- Generate a `drillDownAction` only for work orders where `AssignmentStatus` is not null and not empty:  \n  `drillDownAction`: ora.Invoke(actionResourceAssignmentNav, {OrganizationId, OrganizationCode, WorkOrderNumber})\n- Set `title` as empty.\n\nReturn only the formatted results table. Do not include explanations, lists, extra commentary, or internal identifiers."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Subtitle"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
